Fix the systemd service configuration
Your ZIP extracted the application into:
/opt/devverse/app/app.py

But your systemd service currently points to:
/opt/devverse/app.py

That path is incorrect. If we start the service without fixing it, Python will fail to find app.py.
We also need to correct the working directory.

Install the corrected service file
Run these commands on your application EC2 instance:
sudo cp /opt/devverse/app/systemd/devverse.service \
  /etc/systemd/system/devverse.service

Now create a systemd override:
sudo mkdir -p /etc/systemd/system/devverse.service.d

sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/devverse.service.d/override.conf > /dev/null <<'EOF'
[Service]
WorkingDirectory=/opt/devverse/app
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/opt/devverse/venv/bin/python /opt/devverse/app/app.py
EOF

Reload systemd: sudo systemctl daemon-reload

Verify the final configuration 
sudo systemctl cat devverse

You should see the original service and the override containing:
[Service]
WorkingDirectory=/opt/devverse/app
ExecStart=
ExecStart=/opt/devverse/venv/bin/python /opt/devverse/app/app.py

Do not start the service yet. The application calls init_db() during startup, and we haven't configured its PostgreSQL credentials.


