Install Nginx
First, exit PostgreSQL:

\q

Then return to your application EC2 instance (10.0.76.48), not the database EC2.
Run:
sudo dnf install nginx -y

Verify the installation: nginx -v

Inspect the existing Nginx configuration
Your DevVerse application package already contains an Nginx configuration file.
Let's inspect it before installing it:
cat /opt/devverse/app/nginx/devverse.conf

Also check the website files:
ls -lh /opt/devverse/app/static/


Copy the configuration
Run these commands on your application EC2 (10.0.76.48):
sudo cp /opt/devverse/app/nginx/devverse.conf \
  /etc/nginx/conf.d/devverse.conf

Correct the document root:
sudo sed -i \
  's|root /opt/devverse/static;|root /opt/devverse/app/static;|' \
  /etc/nginx/conf.d/devverse.conf

Check for conflicting Nginx server configurations
Because your DevVerse configuration uses listen 80 default_server, we must ensure another default server isn't already configured.
sudo grep -RnE 'listen[[:space:]]+80|default_server' \
  /etc/nginx/nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/

If /etc/nginx/nginx.conf already defines a default server on port 80, we'll need to resolve that conflict.

Validate the Nginx configuration
sudo nginx -t

Check static-file directory permissions
Nginx must be able to traverse the directories leading to your website files.

namei -l /opt/devverse/app/static/index.html


Fix the Nginx server conflict
Why is this happening?
You currently have two Nginx server configurations:
File	Configuration
/etc/nginx/nginx.conf	Default Nginx server on port 80
/etc/nginx/conf.d/devverse.conf	DevVerse server on port 80

Both use the server name _, which causes the warning.
Our goal is to use the DevVerse configuration as the default web server.

Open the main Nginx configuration
sudo vi /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
Find the existing server block, which should look similar to:
server {
    listen       80;
    listen       [::]:80;
    server_name  _;
    root         /usr/share/nginx/html;

    ...
}

Comment out the entire existing default server { ... } block.

Important: Do not remove the surrounding http { ... } block, the include /etc/nginx/conf.d/*.conf; directive, or other global settings.

Leave the DevVerse configuration in:
/etc/nginx/conf.d/devverse.conf

Validate Nginx again
sudo nginx -t

Start Nginx
systemctl enable --now nginx
systemctl status nginx --no-pager -l

Test the DevVerse website
curl -I http://127.0.0.1/
curl -i http://127.0.0.1/api/health
